{
  "id": "benchmark-c",
  "title": "Integration and concurrency settlement workflow",
  "description": "Idempotency, simultaneous operators, and a retry whose second-timeout recovery is documented only as a transient failure.",
  "files": {
    "requirements.md": "# Settlement integration\n\n## RF-020 Settle a confirmed order\n\nAcceptance criteria:\n\n- Settling a confirmed order marks it Settled and sends one settlement message.\n\n## RF-021 Ignore a repeated settlement\n\nAcceptance criteria:\n\n- A repeated settlement request for the same order is ignored and no second message is sent.\n",
    "integration_notes.md": "# Integration notes\n\nNote INT-1: settlement calls the ledger endpoint with an idempotency key.\nNote INT-2: when two operators settle the same order at the same time the second\nrequest observes the order already Settled.\nNote INT-3: when the ledger endpoint times out the request is retried once; a second\ntimeout leaves the order Confirmed and reports a transient failure.\n"
  },
